# A separate package with its own toolchain and its own CI job.
Chrome-extension/

# HTML is deliberately out of scope.
#
# `scripts/fixtures/` are the pages the integration and accessibility suites
# assert against, and in HTML whitespace IS content: reflowing an element moves
# the text nodes that make up a link's accessible name and everything
# `browser_read_page` extracts. A formatter would quietly rewrite the thing under
# test. `docs/index.html` is the published site page and is hand-kept.
*.html

# Markdown and JSON are deliberately out of scope.
#
# The prose here is hand-wrapped to carry meaning — the shipped skill indexes its
# references BY LINE RANGE, so reflowing a paragraph silently invalidates the
# index that `docs:generate` checks. And README, the two plugin manifests and
# `gemini-extension.json` have machine-written regions; a formatter and a
# generator both rewriting the same bytes is a fight CI would lose every push.
*.md
*.json
